WEBVTT

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:04.140
Who? Who is it?

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:39.240
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:40.810
Lookin' good.

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:47.080
Howard, can't you stand still for a moment?

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:49.890
Just watching you makes me get irritated.

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:52.480
What's that? What about you?

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:54.540
Scowling from morning 'till night.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:57.130
Just seeing your face gets me depressed!

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:58.060
What?

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:00.460
Hey, stop that, both of you.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:03.430
We realize that you're irritated...

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:05.940
...but fighting all the time isn't going to help it.

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:07.930
They don't get tired of it.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:20.900
Today is the tenth day since the blizzard started.

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:26.860
Everyone's stress has piled up after being shut in the cave all day.

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:33.610
And on top of that, because we can't go out to get food, our food and firewood supplies are dwindling.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.150
Luna...

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:36.690
What is it, Adam?

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:39.240
I'm hungry.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:44.260
Bear with it, Adam. We don't have much food left.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:47.000
Then let's burn some more wood.

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:48.240
Adam...

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:50.680
Because it's cold.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:52.140
Shut up!

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:56.190
You're not the only one who's hungry and cold!

00:03:56.260 --> 00:04:00.050
Honestly! Whose fault do you think it is that we're in this situation?

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:01.100
Howard!

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:02.680
But I'm right, aren't I?

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:06.950
If we only hadn't brought this guy back with us, this wouldn't have happened!

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:09.500
Talk about doing something uncalled for.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:17.410
Don't pay it any mind.

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:19.250
It's not your fault, Adam.

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:22.550
Chako, how do things look over there?

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:24.730
This time it looks like it'll work great!

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:26.260
Really?

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:34.590
It seems like this card has a biometric system incorporated into it.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:36.760
Bio... what was that?

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:38.490
Biometrics.

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:41.940
It operates in response to Adam's body.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:45.050
Right now we're putting that information in here.

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:48.050
If we broadcast it, something might happen.

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:50.790
Why are you doing such a tedious thing?

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:53.790
Why don't we just take Adam to the ruins?

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:59.680
You're not suggesting we take Adam out into this blizzard, are you?

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:01.550
When do you think it'll be done?

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:04.510
I think we can have it done by the end of the day.

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:07.510
Then I'll take it there and try it out.

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:10.930
It's impossible in this blizzard! You'll die!

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:15.730
But at this rate we don't know how long we'll have food for.

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:17.080
That may be true...

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:19.810
...but how can we be sure you'll make it to the ruins safely?

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:22.890
We'll go with you.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:26.040
We can't let Luna go alone, can we?

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:27.690
I'll go too.

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:29.110
Everyone...

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:30.910
But...

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:32.410
Menori...

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:37.140
Very well, but don't tempt fate.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:41.000
If anything happens, come back. Promise us that much.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:42.880
I promise.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:44.040
I'll go too!

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:47.300
No way, Adam. You stay here.

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:49.440
But I want to go!

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:51.430
Because... I...

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:54.430
...promise not to be a burden!

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:55.440
Adam...

00:05:56.600 --> 00:06:01.360
Well, If we bring Adam with us, it might help out in case something happens.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:04.810
Okay. Let's go together.

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:25.180
Adam, are you okay?

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:47.640
Everyone, mind your steps!

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:59.080
Chako, are you okay?

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:02.080
My bad. My feet slipped a bit.

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:08.600
We're finally here.

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:26.830
We'd better do somethin' soon.

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:29.490
Will Pague be okay?

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:31.330
I'm sure he's fine.

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:36.430
It's gotten pretty dark.

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:40.210
At this rate, it'll be impossible to reach the ruins by the end of the day.

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:44.830
Anyways, let's hurry. I think we'd best get as far as we can.

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:54.090
I wonder if they're okay.

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:57.460
Give me a break.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.000
How is he?

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:19.960
He's asleep. He's tired, after all.

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:21.730
We should be gettin' to sleep too.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:26.640
You're right. There's still tomorrow.

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:30.990
Pushing yourself...

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:43.210
Who is it?

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:46.360
Alduram Gyet.

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:51.390
Who? Who is it?

00:08:51.610 --> 00:09:03.350
Alduram Gyet.

00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:04.810
Chako!

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:06.650
Snap out of it!

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:09.130
Chako! Chako...

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:12.350
I'm fine...

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:14.080
What's wrong?

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:17.490
Her temperature dropped, and she can't make Hydrogen well.

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:22.360
When they made Chako, they must not have figured she'd ever come somewhere so cold.

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:27.240
Honestly! Whose fault do you think it is that we're in this situation?

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:32.040
If only we hadn't brought this guy back with us, none of this would have happened!

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:34.360
Talk about doing something uncalled for.

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:38.450
Let's get back to the cave for now.

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:41.830
What'cha sayin'? I'm fine.

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:44.530
Hurry up. We gotta get to the ruins.

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:46.930
But... at this rate...

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:49.250
I'm fine.

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:50.980
What should we do, Luna?

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:55.030
Bell, how much longer do you think it'll take to get to the ruins?

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:57.650
I think we can get there in two hours.

00:09:58.100 --> 00:09:59.490
Two hours?

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:17.190
Sorry, Bell.

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:19.030
Don't worry about it.

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:24.500
We'll be at the ruins soon.

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:57.500
No use. Pass me the card.

00:10:57.730 --> 00:10:58.780
Sorry.

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:00.610
Bell, put me down.

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:01.780
But...

00:11:02.110 --> 00:11:03.910
I'm fine now.

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:08.680
I'll help out too.

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:11.530
Then connect that cord to the hole on the bottom.

00:11:16.180 --> 00:11:17.110
Chako!

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:19.700
We hafta do somethin' soon.

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:21.690
Otherwise we'll all die of freezing.

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:30.430
Okay! Now if we broadcast Adam's information, it should open!

00:11:30.990 --> 00:11:31.960
Here we go.

00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:42.610
Okay, looks good, just like that...

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:50.260
Damn, it didn't work!

00:11:51.130 --> 00:11:52.630
Why not?

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:02.790
Why won't it open?

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:06.610
What am I supposed to do?

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:12.430
Chako!

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:18.130
Chako... Chako!

00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:20.900
Chako!

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:23.110
Snap out of it, Chako!

00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:25.660
Chako...

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:27.760
It was pointless after all!

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:29.980
If only we'd gone back to the cave then...

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:32.530
Chako!

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:34.060
Chako...

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:36.910
What's goin' on?

00:12:36.910 --> 00:12:40.960
My name's easier to remember! Chako! Cha-ko!

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:46.180
Chako!

00:13:37.890 --> 00:13:39.460
The door opened...

00:13:51.730 --> 00:13:53.640
Let's hurry into the ruins!

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:55.850
Adam, hurry!

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:57.910
But... Chako...

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:00.540
That's right!

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:05.600
If we use the energy from the cold sleep chamber, we might be able to fix Chako.

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:06.540
Really?

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:08.530
Adam, let's go.

00:14:19.180 --> 00:14:20.940
It's warm in here.

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:25.100
Does it look like we can use the coldsleep energy?

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:26.340
If I can get it working.

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:28.100
I'll check it out.

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:32.110
It's okay. Chako will get better.

00:14:34.780 --> 00:14:36.580
Okay. It's working!

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:38.680
Shingo, how is it?

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:41.750
It's okay. Put Chako down there.

00:14:58.360 --> 00:15:00.540
She'll definitely be fine.

00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:08.490
I wonder if it'll work.

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:09.390
Probably.

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:13.290
Come to think of it, why did the door open?

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:18.580
I'm sure that card was a key to the ruins that only Adam could use.

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:21.010
A key only I can use?

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:22.100
But...

00:15:22.780 --> 00:15:25.360
...why didn't it react at first?

00:15:25.660 --> 00:15:27.360
That's what I don't understand.

00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:30.160
Maybe it understood Adam's feelings.

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:32.600
I just thought of Chako...

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:41.530
Chako! Are you okay?

00:15:47.490 --> 00:15:48.730
Who're you?

00:15:50.230 --> 00:15:52.360
Her memory was reset?

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:56.560
Chako...

00:15:58.550 --> 00:16:01.360
As if! Just kiddin'!

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:03.160
Chako!

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:04.180
What's wrong?

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:06.540
Don't startle me like that!

00:16:07.060 --> 00:16:09.200
Shingo, what happened to me?

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:12.280
Your temperature fell too far and you stopped working.

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:13.660
Stopped working?

00:16:13.960 --> 00:16:16.850
I guess somethin' had to've happened for y'all to've been starin' like that.

00:16:20.860 --> 00:16:21.800
This is--

00:16:22.700 --> 00:16:23.830
We got inside?

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:25.740
Thanks to Adam.

00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:27.010
Adam?

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:29.940
I just...

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:31.330
Thanks a bunch.

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:38.230
All that's left is to stop the infrared inhibitor particles.

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:41.380
Now that we're in the ruins, it's my turn!

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:42.390
Shingo!

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:49.030
It's the thing we saw before.

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:50.340
Chako!

00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:52.400
Yep, just like I thought.

00:16:52.810 --> 00:16:54.090
Did you figure something out?

00:16:54.760 --> 00:16:58.180
These ruins were a terraforming machine after all.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:03.310
These show the terraforming machines on this planet.

00:17:04.930 --> 00:17:07.140
These are all like this?

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:08.490
No doubt.

00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:11.150
That big one is the main computer.

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:14.150
It controls all the terraforming machines.

00:17:14.410 --> 00:17:15.690
What about our island?

00:17:15.690 --> 00:17:16.550
Right here.

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:23.600
It really is this island.

00:17:23.860 --> 00:17:25.180
Fairy Lake is there too.

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:29.830
The main computer is pretty far away.

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:31.810
Can we stop just this machine?

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:35.150
I've been lookin' into that for a while...

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:38.230
...but I can't find the environment control program.

00:17:38.560 --> 00:17:41.490
There's probably a separate control room.

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:43.140
There was nothing along the way.

00:17:43.550 --> 00:17:45.610
Nor in this room.

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:56.340
What's wrong? Adam?

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:07.850
Adam!

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:09.090
I'm fine.

00:18:18.650 --> 00:18:21.240
This is the control room?

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:23.260
Looks like it.

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:27.910
That machine...

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:35.040
I think that's the main switch.

00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:38.230
If we push that, it'll stop?

00:18:38.230 --> 00:18:40.230
Sure will. Let's go, Shingo!

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:48.910
Chako! Shingo!

00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:54.010
Alduram Gyet.

00:18:55.010 --> 00:19:00.090
.ni yats ot uoy rof reisae eb lliw ereh tnemnorivne eht ,nooS

00:19:00.880 --> 00:19:02.900
What's that?

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:09.460
Is this their doing?

00:19:13.810 --> 00:19:15.280
Alduram Gyet.

00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:19.810
.ni yats ot uoy rof reisae eb lliw ereh tnemnorivne eht ,nooS

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:21.910
Alduram Gyet...

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:26.560
"Soon, the environment here will be easier for you to stay in"?

00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:30.950
That's...

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:35.490
Luna! Adam! Out of the way!

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:38.640
Bell!

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:51.460
Bell, are you okay?

00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:54.540
Hurry... the switch...

00:19:54.690 --> 00:19:55.890
I will.

00:19:57.160 --> 00:20:00.880
Adam, it's dangerous, so you stay here. Okay?

00:20:15.350 --> 00:20:16.290
Adam...

00:20:16.290 --> 00:20:18.200
Who are you?

00:20:30.650 --> 00:20:31.660
Luna!

00:20:32.450 --> 00:20:34.030
Alduram Gyet.

00:20:34.030 --> 00:20:38.040
.ni yats ot uoy rof reisae eb lliw ereh tnemnorivne eht ,nooS

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:42.690
What's an environment easier for him to stay in? Adam spends every day shivering!

00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:45.200
Luna!

00:20:48.800 --> 00:20:50.560
Adam!

00:20:54.650 --> 00:20:58.330
What are you doing? Adam's your child, isn't he?

00:21:05.710 --> 00:21:09.160
Adam!

00:21:34.180 --> 00:21:35.640
Adam, are you okay?

00:21:38.680 --> 00:21:39.950
Alduram...

00:21:41.490 --> 00:21:42.950
...Gyet.

00:22:07.480 --> 00:22:08.680
It's stopped!

00:22:09.050 --> 00:22:10.680
I guess it worked out.

00:22:11.860 --> 00:22:13.440
Hey!

00:22:14.150 --> 00:22:15.390
Everyone!

00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:16.810
We're home!

00:22:16.890 --> 00:22:18.010
Luna!

00:22:19.510 --> 00:22:21.010
You were okay!

00:22:21.090 --> 00:22:22.890
Yep, thanks to Adam.

00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:26.080
Well done, Adam.

00:22:27.430 --> 00:22:28.890
I didn't...

00:22:36.350 --> 00:22:37.480
It's the sun!

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:41.860
Yes! The sun! The sun!

00:22:41.860 --> 00:22:43.250
The sun...

00:22:43.780 --> 00:22:46.780
I guess the harsh winter is over.

00:22:47.710 --> 00:22:50.190
I've waited for you, Mr. Sun!

00:22:51.280 --> 00:22:55.930
It's warming up! It's warming up! It's warming up!

00:22:56.860 --> 00:22:59.640
The sun rules!

00:23:03.500 --> 00:23:08.450
Shingo, Chako, and Adam stay the night examining the ruins.

00:23:09.010 --> 00:23:13.440
Yep, although we're mostly interested in the room Adam saw in his dream.

00:23:14.260 --> 00:23:18.540
We have to bet on any chance to get home to the colony.

00:23:18.540 --> 00:23:21.650
We'll back you up. Good luck!

00:23:21.650 --> 00:23:24.650
Right! Leave it to us!

00:23:25.480 --> 00:23:28.140
Next time: For the future
